  "chapter": {
    "number": 26,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "But Job answered and said,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "To whom do you attach yourself, or whom are you going to assist? is it not he that has much strength, and he who has a strong arm?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "To whom have you given counsel? is it not to him who has all wisdom? whom will you follow? is it not one who has the greatest power?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "To whom have you uttered words? and whose breath is it that has come forth from you?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "Shall giants be born from under the water and the inhabitants thereof?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "Hell is naked before him, and destruction has no covering."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "He stretches out the north wind upon nothing, and he upon nothing hangs the earth;"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "binding water in his clouds, and the cloud is not torn under it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "He keeps back the face of his throne, stretching out his cloud upon it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "He has encompassed the face of the water by an appointed ordinance, until the end of light and darkness."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "The pillars of heaven are prostrate and astonished at his rebuke."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          "He has calmed the sea with his might, and by his wisdom the whale has been overthrown."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "And the barriers of heaven fear him, and by a command he has slain the apostate dragon."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "Behold, these are parts of his way; and we will listen to him at the least intimation of his word: but the strength of his thunder who knows, when he shall employ it?"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
